{
  "format": "contentrain-acf-parity@1",
  "mapping_version": 1,
  "site_timezone": "Europe/Istanbul",
  "about": "ACF field → Contentrain field definition and stored value, as both @contentrain/wp-import (acf.ts) and the Contentrain Bridge write it. Owned by wp-import; the Bridge copies this file unchanged and pins the commit it copied.",
  "rules": [
    "`field` is what the site's schema states: the ACF type, and choices, multiple, sub_fields (in schema order) or layouts where the type has them. `value` is the stored value as ACF returns it (image and file with return_format array unless noted).",
    "`site_timezone` is the site's IANA zone (WordPress `timezone_string`); a case's own `site_timezone` overrides it. A date time picker's stored local value is written with the site's UTC offset for that moment, DST included (`2025-03-10T09:30:00+03:00`).",
    "`expect.def` compares type, options, fields (by name, order-free), items and required only; labels, descriptions and field order are each side's own. `null` means the field is not written at all.",
    "`expect.value` is the stored value after conversion; absent means nothing is stored. `expect.dropped` counts values left out because they are outside the stated choices (each side reports them).",
    "Flexible content: one field, rows in order, each row's layout under `layout`; the layout options are every layout the schema declares, sorted, so each case uses them all.",
    "A password field is never read, at any depth, whatever its value.",
    "An empty sub-value (a link's `target: \"\"`) is not written."
  ],
  "not_compared": [
    "References (post_object, relationship, taxonomy, user, gallery, page_link): resolved against each side's own entry ids.",
    "Containers deeper than 2, or holding a reference: the Bridge writes a structured fallback, wp-import types from the value.",
    "Selects inside a repeater, group or layout: REST states no choices for sub-fields.",
    "Fields with no stated type (plain ACF over REST): wp-import types them from the value; the Bridge always has the schema."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "text",
      "field": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "value": "Harbor Co",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "value": "Harbor Co"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "textarea",
      "field": {
        "type": "textarea"
      },
      "value": "Line one\nLine two",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "text"
        },
        "value": "Line one\nLine two"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "wysiwyg",
      "field": {
        "type": "wysiwyg"
      },
      "value": "<p>Built <strong>on time</strong>.</p>",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "richtext"
        },
        "value": "<p>Built <strong>on time</strong>.</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "email",
      "field": {
        "type": "email"
      },
      "value": "hello@harbor.test",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "email"
        },
        "value": "hello@harbor.test"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "url",
      "field": {
        "type": "url"
      },
      "value": "https://harbor.test/",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "url"
        },
        "value": "https://harbor.test/"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "oembed",
      "field": {
        "type": "oembed"
      },
      "value": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aqz-KE-bpKQ",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "url"
        },
        "value": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aqz-KE-bpKQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "number",
      "field": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "value": 250000,
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "value": 250000
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "number stored as a string",
      "field": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "value": "42",
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "value": 42
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "range",
      "field": {
        "type": "range"
      },
      "value": 7,
      "expect": {
        "def": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "value": 7
      }
    },
    {
